From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:52:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the caching file system members in declaration order

CachingFileSystem declares file_system, db and external_file_cache in
that order and its constructor's initializer list names
external_file_cache before db, so the members are initialized in
declaration order whatever the list says and -Wreorder reports the
list as misleading. The list now follows the declaration and the
cache is looked up through the member it initialized, which is the
shape upstream gives the constructor eight commits later; the
initialization is unchanged.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/caching_file_system.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/caching_file_system.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/caching_file_system.cpp
index d98eeb42c5..108da1388e 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/caching_file_system.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/caching_file_system.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ bool ShouldExpandToFillGap(const idx_t current_length, const idx_t added_length)
 } // namespace
 
 CachingFileSystem::CachingFileSystem(FileSystem &file_system_p, DatabaseInstance &db_p)
-    : file_system(file_system_p), external_file_cache(ExternalFileCache::Get(db_p)), db(db_p) {
+    : file_system(file_system_p), db(db_p), external_file_cache(ExternalFileCache::Get(db)) {
 }
 
 CachingFileSystem::~CachingFileSystem() {
